 * A new **AI Controls Panel** (`MaterialCardView`) will be added as an overlay (e.g., top-right) on the `PreviewView` for quick toggling of AI features like Ball Tracking, Player Tracking, and Pose Estimation.
 * The existing `FloatingActionButton` (`nav_button`) will be updated with the new `ic_controls_menu` icon. Its current function will be to eventually open a more comprehensive settings/control panel (likely a BottomSheet in a future step).
 * The older `control_panel` (with camera/scan/stream buttons) and the `tab_layout` with its content will be temporarily removed (commented out) to declutter the main view. This functionality will be re-integrated more elegantly, likely using a BottomSheet, in a subsequent step.
 * The `basic_controls` card (quick record/wicket) will also be removed to simplify the interface, as these actions can be part of the main control panel.

Let's begin by creating the new drawable icons.

