 * The `isNetworkAvailable()` method in your `NetworkUtils` class (after the recent update) does not take a `Context` parameter anymore because `NetworkUtils` itself is instantiated with a `Context`.
 * You need to change the call in `InternationalCricketService.java`:
 * First, ensure `InternationalCricketService` has an instance of `NetworkUtils`.
 ```java
 // In InternationalCricketService.java
 private final NetworkUtils networkUtils;

 private InternationalCricketService(Context context) {
 this.context = context.getApplicationContext();
 this.networkUtils = new NetworkUtils(this.context); // Instantiate NetworkUtils
 // ... rest of constructor
 }
 ```
 * Then, call the method on the instance:
 ```java
 // In loadRankings() or other relevant methods
 if (networkUtils.isNetworkAvailable()) { // Call on the instance
